Z||000004||Black88GT||12-04-2000||09:45 PM||||That is the "dash cover" which I don't think they sell anymore.  I emailed that guy about it after I saw him on ebay, he said it covers over the original dash, not a replacement.<P>Here is what he said to me...<P>"The wood overlay is rosewood from Wood Trim in Florida.  At least that's the way I have them listed.  They do a much better job than the stuff from the FieroStore. <P>The dash is from PISA Corp. in Phoenix, Arizona.  I have linked PISA to CyberCars, the PISA link is on that page.  The Big Fiero Parts Book is also on that page.  The Artero dash is in the book.  The dash is padded and upholstered over a fiberglass base.  It does not replace the original dash which is under the one you can see.  The original is in like new condition but I liked the look of the Artero dash by PISA.  It let me update the car and still keep it looking familiar."<P>I think it looks OK, but like Jeff said (Only2xess) it looks like an 80s Buick Dash.<P>My favorite is the Bonneville Dash on Gary's Customs website.  Can't seem to get any more info. about it other then its a Bonneville Dash.  Looks awesome!!!  If I ever see one in a junkyard I am going to buy the dash in a heartbeat just to give it a try...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
